  "Groups": [
    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "BIT0",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate, the low toggle stage of the 2-bit counter: both inputs read the gate's own committed output C0 through the FANB splitter, so every clock step commits C0' = NAND(C0, C0) = NOT C0 — the bit flips on every step. Designated a register (IsRegister): it holds its committed output through combinational settling and only an explicit clock step samples its inputs and commits new state (D-semantics), which is what makes the feedback loop legal. The whole counter composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation against its threshold 0.125, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here.",
        "Identifier": "group_b8c4033500515d748f4af7609947162b",
        "IdGuid": "cf6f4b33-fde5-5c78-a981-c10b59ddc9cb",
