    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "BIT1",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate, the high toggle stage of the 2-bit counter: it closes the three-NAND XOR, so every clock step commits C1' = NAND(XORA, XORB) = C1 XOR C0 — the high bit toggles exactly when the low bit wraps from 1 to 0. Designated a register (IsRegister): it holds its committed output through combinational settling and only an explicit clock step samples its inputs and commits new state (D-semantics), which is what makes the feedback loop legal. The whole counter composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation against its threshold 0.125, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here.",
        "Identifier": "group_44f444904b5c5c619a0e8398e9fe2cce",
        "IdGuid": "c41bd352-afd9-5694-ae56-a3bb2637e985",
